    {
      "heading": "Reading rules",
      "text": [
        "The built-in vowel অ is said ɔ in most places (কর kɔr), o when the next syllable has i or u (নদী nodi, but মন্দির mɔndir with its closed syllable), and is often dropped at the end of a word (নাম nam, not namɔ) and in the middle of longer words. The pronunciation under each word shows which.",
        "ই/ঈ and উ/ঊ are spelling distinctions only: they sound the same.",
        "Stress is light and falls on the first syllable; the IPA marks it with ˈ."
      ]
    },
